### Electron Version

42.2.0

### What operating system(s) are you using?

macOS

### Operating System Version

macOS 14.7

### Expected Behavior

All bytes in the local record fixture are returned.

### Actual Behavior

The custom memo scheme returns only the first half of the binary record. This is the handler function:

```js
const fs = require("node:fs/promises");
async function serveRecord(request) {
  const bytes = await fs.readFile(fixturePath);
  return new Response(bytes, {
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/octet-stream" }
  });
}
```

### Testcase Gist URL

_No response_

### Additional Information

Elsewhere the app registers serveRecord using protocol.handle("memo", serveRecord). fixturePath points to a proprietary record file. I have not supplied that file, a substitute buffer, the registration setup or the requesting page.
